# External Integrations

External providers that are reusable by multiple applications or bounded contexts belong in a dedicated integrations library. Do not put business-specific providers in `libs/shared`.

## Placement Rules

- Put reusable external providers in `libs/integrations/src/{capability}/{provider}`.
- Put context-specific adaptation in `domains/{context}/src/infrastructure/external/{capability}`.
- Put generic technical infrastructure in `libs/shared/src/{messaging|storage|http|observability}`.
- Put operational infrastructure in root `infrastructure/`.

## Responsibilities

`libs/integrations` may contain:

- provider HTTP clients or SDK wrappers;
- provider authentication and technical config;
- raw provider request/response types;
- provider error mapping;
- mappers to neutral integration contracts;
- generic provider retry/circuit-breaker behavior.

`libs/integrations` must not contain:

- bounded context entities;
- business decisions such as when to charge, approve, refund, issue, or cancel;
- product-specific pricing, fraud, voucher, order, or customer rules;
- public API DTOs from an application.

## Context Adaptation

Use `domains/{context}/src/infrastructure/external/{capability}` for:

- selecting a provider for that context;
- mapping context commands/results to neutral integration inputs/outputs;
- composing provider calls with context policies;
- provider-specific configuration that is owned by the context.

## Examples

```txt
libs/integrations/src/payment/fourall/
libs/integrations/src/payment/paymee/
libs/integrations/src/antifraud/clearsale/
libs/integrations/src/seating/seatsio/
libs/integrations/src/wallet/google-wallet/

domains/ordering/src/infrastructure/external/payment/
domains/ordering/src/infrastructure/external/antifraud/
domains/catalog/src/infrastructure/external/seating/
```

## Naming

- Use `{provider}-{capability}.provider.ts` for provider implementations.
- Use `{provider}-{capability}.client.ts` for low-level API clients when separated.
- Use `{provider}-{capability}.mapper.ts` for provider contract mapping.
- Use `{provider}-{capability}.types.ts` for provider-specific types.
